{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rectorphp/rector/releases/404491207","assets_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rectorphp/rector/releases/404491207/assets","upload_url":"https://uploads.github.com/repos/rectorphp/rector/releases/404491207/assets{?name,label}","html_url":"https://github.com/rectorphp/rector/releases/tag/2.7.0","id":404491207,"author":{"login":"TomasVotruba","id":924196,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjkyNDE5Ng==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/924196?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/TomasVotruba","html_url":"https://github.com/TomasVotruba","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TomasVotruba/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TomasVotruba/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TomasVotruba/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TomasVotruba/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TomasVotruba/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TomasVotruba/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TomasVotruba/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TomasVotruba/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TomasVotruba/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"node_id":"RE_kwDOBczZKc4YHAvH","tag_name":"2.7.0","target_commitish":"main","name":"Released Rector 2.7","draft":false,"immutable":false,"prerelease":false,"created_at":"2026-10-06T08:46:47Z","updated_at":"2026-10-06T08:47:12Z","published_at":"2026-10-06T08:47:00Z","assets":[],"tarball_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rectorphp/rector/tarball/2.7.0","zipball_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rectorphp/rector/zipball/2.7.0","body":"## New Rules :sparkles:\r\n\r\n- Add `TernaryToNullsafeCoalesceRector` ([#8499](https://github.com/rectorphp/rector-src/pull/8499))\r\n- Add `BoolReturnTypeFromBooleanConstAndStrictReturnsRector` for mixed const + strict bool returns ([#8498](https://github.com/rectorphp/rector-src/pull/8498))\r\n- Add `ConstructorReadonlyAssignToDefaultRector` for readonly property defaults ([#8502](https://github.com/rectorphp/rector-src/pull/8502))\r\n- Add `RemoveOverriddenAssignBeforeIfElseRector` ([#8505](https://github.com/rectorphp/rector-src/pull/8505))\r\n\r\n<br>\r\n\r\n## Performance Improvements :rocket:\r\n\r\n- Cache class-like name resolution per file version in `ShortNameResolver`, so name import no longer rescans the whole file for every name - up to ~24 % fewer CPU instructions on large projects ([#8524](https://github.com/rectorphp/rector-src/pull/8524))\r\n- Cache dry-run files whose `FileDiff` has no content change ([#8523](https://github.com/rectorphp/rector-src/pull/8523))\r\n- Key the file cache on project-relative paths, so a cache survives a change of checkout ([#8490](https://github.com/rectorphp/rector-src/pull/8490))\r\n- Use `FileSystem::writeAtomic()` in `FileCacheStorage` to avoid partial cache reads on parallel runs ([#8520](https://github.com/rectorphp/rector-src/pull/8520))\r\n- Terminate timed-out and unconnected workers ([#8522](https://github.com/rectorphp/rector-src/pull/8522))\r\n- Fix silently skipped files when the only worker is respawned ([#8521](https://github.com/rectorphp/rector-src/pull/8521))\r\n- Give the worker the same NDJSON frame limit as the main process ([#8489](https://github.com/rectorphp/rector-src/pull/8489))\r\n- Bump to PHPStan 2.3\r\n\r\n<br>\r\n\r\n## Bugfixes :bug:\r\n\r\n- `RenamePropertyRector`: rename the property both in the trait and in the class property itself ([#8518](https://github.com/rectorphp/rector-src/pull/8518))\r\n- `RenameClassRector`: throw on same old and new class in the configuration ([#8515](https://github.com/rectorphp/rector-src/pull/8515))\r\n- `ScalarParamTypeByMethodCallTypeRector`: skip string param inference to avoid unsafe scalar coercion ([#8514](https://github.com/rectorphp/rector-src/pull/8514))\r\n- `RepeatedAndNotEqualToNotInArrayRector` / `RepeatedOrEqualToInArrayRector`: skip short-circuit dependent values ([#8516](https://github.com/rectorphp/rector-src/pull/8516))\r\n- `SeparateMultiUseImportsRector`: keep trait `use` adaptations ([#8510](https://github.com/rectorphp/rector-src/pull/8510))\r\n- `Privatize*Rector`: drop the `final` flag when changing `protected` to `private`, since `private final` is forbidden on PHP 8.4 ([#8509](https://github.com/rectorphp/rector-src/pull/8509))\r\n- `AddNameToBooleanArgumentRector` / `AddNameToNullArgumentRector`: skip callees marked `@no-named-arguments` ([#8508](https://github.com/rectorphp/rector-src/pull/8508))\r\n- `TypedPropertyFromStrictConstructorRector`: skip a protected property redeclared in a child class ([#8503](https://github.com/rectorphp/rector-src/pull/8503))\r\n- `RemoveAlwaysTrueIfConditionRector`: skip a maybe-undefined variable ([#8501](https://github.com/rectorphp/rector-src/pull/8501))\r\n- `SingularSwitchToIfRector`: skip nested `break`/`continue` in the case body ([#8500](https://github.com/rectorphp/rector-src/pull/8500))\r\n- `TypeDeclaration`: skip redundant intersection types in union return types ([#8527](https://github.com/rectorphp/rector-src/pull/8527))\r\n- Naming: keep mass nouns ending in `data`/`info` untouched when singularizing ([#8492](https://github.com/rectorphp/rector-src/pull/8492))\r\n\r\n<br>\r\n\r\n## rector-doctrine :orange_circle:\r\n\r\n- Add `DoctrineQueryBuilderSortDirectionRector` ([#524](https://github.com/rectorphp/rector-doctrine/pull/524))\r\n- Add `DoctrineOrderByAttributeSortDirectionRector` ([#525](https://github.com/rectorphp/rector-doctrine/pull/525))\r\n- Register the SortDirection rules in the composer-based set and cover `Expr\\OrderBy::add()` ([#530](https://github.com/rectorphp/rector-doctrine/pull/530))\r\n- `CorrectDefaultTypesOnEntityPropertyRector`: support properties initialized as `int` ([#526](https://github.com/rectorphp/rector-doctrine/pull/526))\r\n\r\n<br>\r\n\r\n## rector-symfony :musical_note:\r\n\r\n- `GetRequestRector`: reuse an existing untyped `$request` param ([#1066](https://github.com/rectorphp/rector-symfony/pull/1066))\r\n- `CommandConfigureToAttributeRector`: do not report a change when nothing is extracted ([#1068](https://github.com/rectorphp/rector-symfony/pull/1068))\r\n- Fix `PhpAstExtractor` import removal in the composer-based Symfony set ([#1070](https://github.com/rectorphp/rector-symfony/pull/1070))\r\n\r\n<br>\r\n\r\n## rector-phpunit :green_circle:\r\n\r\n- Add `WillReturnCallbackFallbackToReturnFalseRector` ([#784](https://github.com/rectorphp/rector-phpunit/pull/784))\r\n- Extend `FlipAssertRector` to more assert methods and expected value shapes ([#787](https://github.com/rectorphp/rector-phpunit/pull/787))\r\n- `AllowMockObjectsForDataProviderRector`: skip stub-only `->method()` calls ([#790](https://github.com/rectorphp/rector-phpunit/pull/790))\r\n- Fix changing keys of data providers for tests with optional arguments ([#783](https://github.com/rectorphp/rector-phpunit/pull/783))\r\n- Deprecate `ConfiguredMockEntityToSetterObjectRector` as experimental ([#789](https://github.com/rectorphp/rector-phpunit/pull/789))\r\n","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rectorphp/rector/releases/404491207/reactions","total_count":5,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":2,"confused":0,"heart":3,"rocket":0,"eyes":0}}